      "leadSummary": "Microbiology studies organisms and biological entities that are usually too small to characterize unaided, but scale is not a sound definition of an evolutionary group. Bacteria, archaea, microscopic eukaryotes and fungi differ profoundly in cellular architecture and descent. Viruses, which are acellular and require ho"
